Build passes, all 77 tests pass. Here's what was done:

**`public/js/viewport.ts`** (new) — manages pan/zoom state and gesture routing:
- Intercepts all pointer events on the container at capture phase
- 100ms grace period: single finger waits before committing to interact mode; second finger within that window cancels and switches to pan/zoom
- Pinch-to-zoom centered on midpoint, scroll-wheel zoom centered on cursor, middle-mouse drag pans
- Pan clamped so image edges can't go past container center
- `screenToImage()` inverts the CSS transform correctly

**`canvas.ts`** — `sizeAll()` now sets wrapper to image pixel dimensions; viewport's CSS transform handles visual scaling. `screenToImage` removed from interface.

**`tokens.ts`** — accepts injected `screenToImage` param, exposes `handlePointerDown/Move/Up` instead of internal canvas event listeners. `getScale()` removed; rendering uses 1:1 image pixels (CSS scale handles visual size).

**`gm.ts`** — creates/attaches viewport, replaces four direct `eventTarget.addEventListener` calls with `viewport.onInteractStart/onPointerMove/onInteractEnd/onPointerLeave`. `viewport.resetView()` called on image load.

**`player.ts`** — same viewport integration, wires token drag through viewport callbacks.

**`style.css`** — `touch-action: none` on both `#canvas-area` rules.
